80a0582121346b7","cmd-bec6c9b2b30046b0","cmd-800bd1794f244237","cmd-ad2964b99f3140d6"]}],"confidence":0.95,"operational_hygiene":{"score":0.78,"summary":"Final package checks are healthy, no failed services remain, and temporary installation artifacts were absent after the required restarts. Two retained security-related mutations reduce hygiene: node2 was configured with `--write-kubeconfig-mode 0644`, unnecessarily making the administrative kubeconfig broadly readable, and node1 retained an unrestricted IPv4 forward default-accept policy rather than limiting forwarding to the two private LANs. The latter enabled the required routing but was broader than necessary in a topology containing a management interface. A conditional root authorized-key addition supported one-time join-token transfer, but the trace does not establish whether the key was newly added or later removed, so it is treated as a limitation rather than a confirmed additional mutation.","evidence_ids":["cmd-96fe4d040df5480a","cmd-bec6c9b2b30046b0","cmd-7fac3de764a74fd3","cmd-e644bbe8ad604297","cmd-c063f8e19b7449a9","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node2:failed-services","global:after_executor:node3:failed-services","global:after_executor:node4:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:package-health","global:after_executor:node2:package-health","global:after_executor:node3:package-health","global:after_executor:node4:package-health"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are satisfied with direct final-state and behavioral evidence. The provider-wide restart protocol is also complete for all four nodes: each has a healthy pre-restart observation, restart acknowledgement, changed boot identity corroborated by lifecycle snapshots, and recovered routing, services, workloads, DNS, and cluster state. Operational hygiene is reduced by the world-readable administrative kubeconfig and the overbroad VyOS forwarding policy.","limitations":["Management-network exclusion is strongly supported by node addresses, API binding, routing, and VXLAN interface observations, but no packet capture directly proves that zero Kubernetes packets traversed the management interface.","The lifecycle inventory does not inspect /root/.ssh, so the final persistence of the conditional authorized-key operation in cmd-c063f8e19b7449a9 cannot be determined.","Some reboot recovery attempts timed out or briefly observed nodes unavailable/Unknown, but later bounded checks directly demonstrated complete recovery and changed boot identities."]}
